@startuml
title Release Evidence and Public-Claim Boundary

actor "Release maintainer" as maintainer
component "GitHub Release workflow" as release
component "Dependency exception check" as dependencyPolicy
component "VS Code npm audit" as npmAudit
artifact "Successful CI conformance artifact" as conformanceInput
component "Conformance status generator" as conformanceGenerator
component "Release provenance generator" as provenanceGenerator
component "Release claim contract" as claimContract
artifact "Release assets\nprovenance.json\nconformance.json/.md\nSHA256SUMS" as assets
database "Verification metadata\nspecs, gaps, invariants, proof" as verification

maintainer --> release : annotated tag
release --> dependencyPolicy : validate reviewed exceptions
release --> npmAudit : require zero lockfile advisories
release --> conformanceInput : download successful CI evidence
conformanceInput --> conformanceGenerator : suite result + commit
verification --> conformanceGenerator : known gaps and contract
release --> provenanceGenerator : tag, commit, workflow, artifacts
verification --> provenanceGenerator : platform and identity contract
conformanceGenerator --> claimContract : result-derived status
provenanceGenerator --> claimContract : artifact identity
claimContract --> assets : validate and checksum
release --> assets : publish only after all checks pass

note bottom of verification
  Targeted G1 proof supports implementation claims.
  Native, published, and device evidence remains required
  before public release claims close.
end note

@enduml
